      {
        "width": 48,
        "height": 16,
        "widget": {
          "title": "What is RUM?",
          "text": {
            "content": "# Real User Monitoring (RUM)\nReal user monitoring, often abbreviated as __RUM__, is a type of performance monitoring that captures and analyzes each transaction by users of an application. It provides insights into how end-users interact with an app, their experiences, and any issues they encounter.\n \n## Objective\nThe primary objective of this initiative is to leverage Real User Monitoring (RUM) to analyze API requests and gain valuable insights into customer usage patterns.\n \n## Scope\nRUM is typically employed to analyze GUI workflows and online content streaming. However, in the context of GCNV, we are utilizing RUM to analyze API requests and extract meaningful insights.\n \n## Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)\nWe have collected the following key metrics (non-exhaustive list):\n \n1. Top customer operations\n2. Top API requests (features)\n3. Volumes created with LV, AT, service levels, capacity, etc.\n4. Trends in Replication and Backup enabled operations\n5. Time-of-day operations\n6. Update operations",
            "format_": 1,
            "style": {
              "background_color": "#FFFFFF",
              "text_color": "#212121",
              "horizontal_alignment": 1,
              "vertical_alignment": 1,
              "padding": 1,
              "font_size": 4,
              "pointer_location": 0
            }
          },
          "id": ""
        },
        "x_pos": 0,
        "y_pos": 0
      },
